"A pezyva is an Artonan sleeveless outer vest that opens in front, usually without a collar."
"Its closure runs diagonally, leaving one side's waist and hip free for pouches or tools."
"Two triangular tails hang over the other thigh."
"Embroidering a commendation onto one is 'clothing oneself with the honor'."
"Artonans always read meaning in clothes, even on humans; bare necks can be read many ways."
"A humble visitor should not wear a fully educated wizard's whole ensemble."
